{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1426818-aberrant-what-sorts-of-new-consumer-technology-exists-in-2028","id":1426818,"title":"[Aberrant] What sorts of new consumer technology exists in 2028?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-01T06:28:26-08:00","id":1426818,"title":"[Aberrant] What sorts of new consumer technology exists in 2028?","content":"Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is not our future, but we can definitely make some extrapolations. Novas have changed the world and technology, but what does that mean to the average person? Here are the ideas I have and evidence from the text so far.<br /> <br /> Advanced Drones - Slider is given one of these by her teammates.<br /> Faster, better networks<br /> Further expanding of social media and online platforms<br /> Flying cars (not really consumer but)<br /> <br /> What else is different? Obviously things are better, but what is going to be commonplace then that isn't now. Has AR become widespread yet? Are drones delivering packages directly to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T07:09:03-08:00","id":1426824,"title":"","content":"I think the book mentions tools that can be quickly transformed into other tools. Might be nice to own one tool that can replace most of a toolbox.<br /> <br /> I imagine that average person in many regions can easily afford a cheap electric car that's self-driving, costs almost nothing to recharge, and can run for an incredibly long distance before running down the batteries. And seat belts and other safety systems are probably more effective. Cities would probably have improved mass transit instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T17:30:15-08:00","id":1426886,"title":"","content":"Also things like fast and convenient dental treatments. Say, some coretech spray on treatment that deals with cavities. <br /> <br /> For the elderly, more advanced sensors that can pick up dangerous issues before they become critical. Grandpa goes to bed, and then at 9, the firedepartment is there because his bedside sensor detected an incoming stroke. <br /> <br /> Spray on lights that run from ambient body heat or store energy during teh day, giving light at night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T19:08:26-08:00","id":1426895,"title":"","content":"With the spread of eufiber, cheap room temperature superconductors and cheap high capacity batteries are a thing, so expect portable electronics to last much longer between charges, and for computational power to skyrocket. Your phone probably stores more data in itself (rather than in the cloud) than a modern high end desktop. A tablet probably has enough processing capacity to match the CGI of the original Iron Man movie, so expect the equivalent of programming script kiddies to be pumping out near professional quality effects on their YouTube channels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T23:08:42-08:00","id":1426927,"title":"","content":"Also, some nova has probably figured out how to ruin current forms of cryptocurrencies, so consumers benefit from never having to hear about bitcoin again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T07:19:24-08:00","id":1426976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/tri